# Upstream: github.com/<your-github-username>/claudes-markdown-12-rules/.gitignore
# Everything above the scaffold block below is that file, verbatim. Re-pull it
# rather than hand-editing here, so one project's fix reaches every project.

# Dependencies
**/node_modules/

# Lock files (never change, never need context)
**/package-lock.json
**/go.sum
**/poetry.lock
**/Cargo.lock

# Build output
**/dist/
**/.next/
**/build/
**/target/

# Binary / compiled
**/bin/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Stale branches
**/.worktrees/

# IDE / cache
**/.superpowers/
**/.claude/agents/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/node_modules/.cache

# Test coverage / reports
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/
**/htmlcov/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Env files (security + noise)
**/.env*
!**/.env.example

# Logs
**/*.log
**/logs/

# Terraform state / cache / secrets
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.backup
**/*.tfvars
!**/*.tfvars.example

# Docker layer cache
**/.dockercache/

# Python venvs
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Temp / scratch
**/tmp/
**/temp/

# Vim swap files
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*.un~

# OS noise
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- project-scaffold ------------------------------------------------------
# Not upstream's concern: the files this skill's tools create.

# agent cache - derived, rebuildable, never authoritative
.claude/cache/

# local settings - machine-specific paths, recreated by scaffold.sh
.claude/settings.local.json

# lock files used by the scaffold tools
.issues.lock
.backlog.lock
